{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1183235-which-legion","id":1183235,"title":"Which Legion...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-07T06:16:17-08:00","id":1183235,"title":"Which Legion...","content":"Would my character find themselves in based on the following circumstances of their death: having been falsely imprisoned for the type of crime that would make even a hardened criminal sick to their stomach, and with no prospect of parole and being abandoned by everyone he loved, he ultimately became suicidal. Now, on the date that he was due to carry out the act, several of his fellow prisoners would gang up on him and ultimately beat and shank him to death. Now then, a violent death would land him within the Grim Legion, but given that he had completely given up on life, he wanted to die anyways, that sentiment could land him in the Silent Legion...unless there's something else that I've missed.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11607-irontsim","name":"Irontsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11607_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T07:03:21-08:00","id":1183252,"title":"","content":"Hm. He's one of those I think both could lay a claim to - his life was ended by violence, but ended <i>in</i> despair. It's worth considering whether he primarily wants revenge for what happened to him, which would make him a good fit for the Grim, or whether he's more interested in dealing with the fact everything still isn't over, in engaging with his issues, which would direct him towards the Silent.<br /> <br /> If he allowed himself to be killed, that'd pretty much push him to the Silent.<br /> <br /> If the other two couldn't decide, he might go to the Paupers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T10:32:50-08:00","id":1183299,"title":"","content":"Since he was put in the position of being both suicidal and murdered by being framed, then the desire to find out who set him up in the first place could easily qualify him for the Beggar's Legion. (There is president for this sort of thing; Gen. Patton's write up in Hierarchy mentions his joining the Beggar's Legion because of the questions surrounding the auto accident which lead to his death.)<br /> <br /> He may also qualify for the Penitent Legion, given his broken mental state upon death and, arguably, the twin insanities of the corruption of the justice system and savagery of prison culture. <br /> <br /> And, depending on ultimate circumstances behind his death, the fall out if his death and if public discovery of his being innocent would impact society, and the irony of being murdered the day you decide to kill yourself may all potentially qualify him for the Legion of Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 02-07-2018, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T16:31:43-08:00","id":1183423,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I could see Grim, Silent, or Pauper. It really all comes down to who offers the best bribe to the character\u2019s Reaper.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T17:50:19-08:00","id":1183446,"title":"","content":"What everyone else said. If it were me, I'd have my character yoinked into the Paupers because the whiny Beggar Lord is easily the most interesting Deathlord. But yes, as others have said, consider what kind of personal quest your character could go on, which could be supported with Legion resources. Revenge? Then he should hope to land with the Grim. Transcendence or moving on from what happened? Silent. Investigating circumstances of death? Pauper.<br /> <br /> Might also be interesting to land in the &quot;wrong&quot; legion and take the initiative to switch legions, or be stolen by a recruiter after being offered the resources and access that better suit him.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T04:48:37-08:00","id":1184699,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of leeway here. Most important of all: which Legion do you *want* him to be a part of?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}